    "description": "This dataset contains oceanographic data collected in and around Hawaii, the US EEE, and in the High Seas around the Musicians Seamounts. Operations for this cruise were conducted 24 hours/day and consisted of daily remotely operated vehicle (ROV), overnight mapping, and full shore-based participation via telepresence. Operations included the use of the ship\u00e2\u0080\u0099s deep-water mapping system, XBT and CTD casts in support of multibeam sonar mapping operations, OER\u00e2\u0080\u0099s two-body ROV Deep Discoverer and Seirios, and the ship\u00e2\u0080\u0099s high-bandwidth satellite connection for continuous real-time ship-to-shore communications. Data acquisition from shipboard sensors includes navigation data, meteorological data (wind, air temperature, relative humidity, barometric pressure), and oceanographic data (thermosalinograph, sound velocity probe, bathythermograph). Operations also included the use of the ship\u00e2\u0080\u0099s Acoustic Doppler Current Profilers (ADCP).",
